WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.933
Here's why this matters: the series
moves four populations to the cloud,

2
00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:08.300
each on its own track, and
this book is the HR track.

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.425
It's about people.

4
00:00:09.425 --> 00:00:13.842
Employee accounts follow the HR
record; contractor accounts follow the

5
00:00:13.842 --> 00:00:18.038
contractor source of authority,
which is still the agency's decision.

6
00:00:18.038 --> 00:00:22.926
Joining, moving and leaving then
change access by rule, not by ticket.

7
00:00:22.926 --> 00:00:27.220
You'll know you're there when every
enabled account matches an authoritative

8
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:31.113
record or an owned exception, and no
hand-kept group membership is left.

9
00:00:31.113 --> 00:00:36.222
Devices and servers are in Devices
and Endpoints; service accounts and AI

10
00:00:36.222 --> 00:00:41.750
agents are in Identity and Directory, Data
Platform, and AI Identity Governance.

11
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:45.026
And the design supports the
federal account-management

12
00:00:45.026 --> 00:00:48.162
and personnel controls; it
doesn't close them on its own.

13
00:00:48.162 --> 00:00:49.920
Now, what access runs on.
